# Local reference material is deliberately kept out of the repo. CLAUDE.md is the
# spec of record, and its scanner-spec section is the distillation of any
# predecessor/reference source — keeping originals in-tree invites a future
# session to consult them instead of the brief. That's the drift we closed off.
reference/

# Transient test-harness artifacts (created + removed by the gates; never committed).
tests/.swbump
tests/.zxing.tmp

# REAL USER DATA. The repo is public-facing and fixture-synthetic forever (CLAUDE.md),
# so an actual export -- barcodes, meals, weights, sleep, BP, fasting history -- must
# never be committable. Kept in-tree because the evaluation set is built from it, and
# ignored so that decision cannot be undone by a stray `git add -A`.
export.json
export*.json
*.export.json

# The evaluation set is DERIVED from that export -- product names, barcodes and what
# was eaten on which day. The generator (eval/build.py) is committable; its output is
# the user's eating history in another shape and is not. Whether it ever becomes
# public is the user's call, not a default.
eval/set.json
